{"step_index":9882,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T13:28:10Z","thinking":"Planning the `gemini_vision_extractor.py` module, the core functions are: a file hash computation (SHA-256) and a strategy for controlled cache storage. The file hash serves as a unique identifier for PDF files. Organized cache storage prevents haphazard temporary file placement.\n\n\nThe system will establish a consistent cache structure based on process context or a fallback directory outside the process space if needed. A manifest file will track processing status and page completion, enabling quick resumption from prior work. The extraction will first attempt to load fully cached results for immediate return.\n\nIf a full cache isn't available, pending pages, those missing results or needing WebP rendering, are identified. WebP images will be generated if not present, and then results will be gathered for the identified pending pages.\n\n\nNow focusing on processing image data, preparing to send requests to an image analysis endpoint with base64 encoded image data and a specific prompt designed for pharmaceutical extraction. The response will be parsed as JSON, validated for the presence of extracted items, and then saved to a designated file. Page completion is tracked and the manifest updated accordingly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nGemini Vision Extraction Engine.\nExtracts pharmaceutical items from PDF files page-by-page using Google AI Studio Vision Gateway.\nFeatures:\n- WebP high-resolution compressed rendering (pypdfium2 at scale 2.5)\n- Process-isolated structured cache (manifest.json, pages/, results/)\n- Full resume & interruption capability (resumes from incomplete page)\n- SHA-256 fingerprinting for instant cache reloads\n\"\"\"\n\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport pypdfium2 as pdfium\nimport requests\n\n\ndef _compute_file_hash(filepath: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Computes SHA-256 checksum of a file.\"\"\"\n    hasher = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n        while chunk := f.read(65536):\n            hasher.update(chunk)\n    return hasher.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _get_cache_dir(filepath: Path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds or creates an organized cache directory for this file.\n    If the file is inside a process folder (data/processes/PROC-XXX),\n    places cache under data/processes/PROC-XXX/cache/vision/<file_slug>_<hash[:10]>.\n    Otherwise places it under <parent>/.vision_cache/<file_slug>_<hash[:10]>.\n    \"\"\"\n    filepath = Path(filepath).resolve()\n    file_hash = _compute_file_hash(filepath)\n    file_slug = re.sub(r\"[^\\w\\-]\", \"_\", filepath.stem)[:25]\n    folder_name = f\"{file_slug}_{file_hash[:10]}\"\n\n    # Check if inside a process directory\n    parts = filepath.parts\n    proc_idx = -1\n    for i, p in enumerate(parts):\n        if p.startswith(\"PROC-\"):\n            proc_idx = i\n            break\n\n    if proc_idx != -1:\n        proc_root = Path(*parts[:proc_idx + 1])\n        cache_dir = proc_root / \"cache\" / \"vision\" / folder_name\n    else:\n        cache_dir = filepath.parent / \".vision_cache\" / folder_name\n\n    (cache_dir / \"pages\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (cache_dir / \"results\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    return cache_dir\n\n\ndef _clean_json_response(raw_text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Cleans markdown fences or surrounding noise to extract valid JSON.\"\"\"\n    text = raw_text.strip()\n    # Strip markdown codeblocks\n    if \"```\" in text:\n        match = re.search(r\"```(?:json)?\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*```\", text)\n        if match:\n            text = match.group(1).strip()\n\n    # Find enclosing json object\n    start = text.find(\"{\")\n    end = text.rfind(\"}\")\n    if start != -1 and end != -1 and end > start:\n        text = text[start:end+1]\n\n    return json.loads(text)\n\n\ndef extract_items_from_pdf_vision(\n    filepath: Path,\n    api_url: str = \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1/chat/completions\",\n    api_key: str = \"[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]\",\n    model: str = \"gemini-3.8-flash\",\n    scale: float = 2.5,\n    quality: int = 85,\n    max_retries: int = 3,\n) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all drug items from a PDF using page-by-page Gemini Vision.\n    Supports smart resumption and isolated disk caching.\n    \"\"\"\n    filepath = Path(filepath)\n    if not filepath.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"PDF file not found: {filepath}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n    print(f\"[*] [VISION EXTRACTOR] File: {filepath.name}\")\n    print(f\"{'='*60}\")\n\n    file_hash = _compute_file_hash(filepath)\n    cache_dir = _get_cache_dir(filepath)\n    manifest_path = cache_dir / \"manifest.json\"\n\n    # Read PDF metadata\n    pdf = pdfium.PdfDocument(filepath)\n    total_pages = len(pdf)\n    print(f\"  -> Total pages: {total_pages}\")\n    print(f\"  -> Cache location: {cache_dir.relative_to(filepath.parents[3]) if len(filepath.parents) >= 4 else cache_dir}\")\n\n    # Load or initialize manifest\n    manifest = {\n        \"file_name\": filepath.name,\n        \"file_hash\": file_hash,\n        \"total_pages\": total_pages,\n        \"completed_pages\": [],\n        \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n        \"created_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n        \"updated_at\": datetime.now().isoformat()\n    }\n\n    if manifest_path.exists():\n        try:\n            with open(manifest_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                loaded_manifest = json.load(f)\n            if loaded_manifest.get(\"file_hash\") == file_hash and loaded_manifest.get(\"total_pages\") == total_pages:\n                manifest = loaded_manifest\n                print(f\"  -> Found existing cache manifest (Completed pages: {len(manifest.get('completed_pages', []))}/{total_pages})\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"  [!] Could not parse manifest, re-initializing: {e}\")\n\n    # Check if completely finished\n    completed_set = set(manifest.get(\"completed_pages\", []))\n    all_pages_cached = (len(completed_set) == total_pages and \n                        all((cache_dir / \"results\" / f\"page_{p}.json\").exists() for p in range(1, total_pages + 1)))\n\n    if all_pages_cached:\n        print(f\"[+] All {total_pages} pages previously extracted in cache. Loading instantly...\")\n        all_items = []\n        for p in range(1, total_pages + 1):\n            res_file = cache_dir / \"results\" / f\"page_{p}.json\"\n            with open(res_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                p_data = json.load(f)\n                items = p_data.get(\"items\", [])\n                for it in items:\n                    it[\"source_file\"] = filepath.name\n                    if \"source_page\" not in it:\n                        it[\"source_page\"] = p\n                all_items.extend(items)\n        print(f\"[+] Loaded {len(all_items)} items from cache in 0.05s.\")\n        return all_items\n\n    # Process pending pages\n    print(f\"[*] Starting/Resuming Vision extraction across {total_pages} page(s)...\")\n\n    for page_num in range(1, total_pages + 1):\n        page_res_path = cache_dir / \"results\" / f\"page_{page_num}.json\"\n        page_img_path = cache_dir / \"pages\" / f\"page_{page_num}.webp\"\n\n        # Check if this page is already completed\n        if page_num in completed_set and page_res_path.exists():\n            print(f\"  -> [Page {page_num}/{total_pages}] Already in cache, skipping extraction.\")\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"\\n  -> [Page {page_num}/{total_pages}] Rendering & extracting...\")\n\n        # 1. Render page to WebP if image does not exist\n        if not page_img_path.exists():\n            page_obj = pdf[page_num - 1]\n            img = page_obj.render(scale=scale).to_pil()\n            img.save(page_img_path, format=\"WEBP\", quality=quality)\n            print(f\"     [+] Rendered WebP: {page_img_path.stat().st_size / 1024:.1f} KB\")\n\n        # 2. Read image as Base64\n        with open(page_img_path, \"rb\") as f:\n            img_b64 = base64.b64encode(f.read()).decode(\"utf-8\")\n\n        # 3. Prompt setup\n        prompt = (\n            \"أنت خبير صيدلي متخصص في استخراج بيانات فواتير وقوائم الأدوية.\\n\"\n            \"قم باستخراج جميع أسماء الأدوية والمنتجات الطبية الموجودة في هذه الصورة بدقة كاملة.\\n\"\n            \"القواعد الصارمة:\\n\"\n            \"1. استخرج كل صنف أو سطر منتج دوائي يظهر في الصورة كعنصر مستقل.\\n\"\n            \"2. انقل اسم الصنف كاملاً كما هو في الصورة بالضبط في (item_name_raw) مع الاحتفاظ بالاسم والتركيز والهيئة الدوائية والشركة.\\n\"\n            \"3. تجنب تصحيح الأخطاء الإملائية أو ترجمة الكلمات أو تغيير الأرقام. احتفظ بالأرقام الموجودة داخل الاسم.\\n\"\n            \"4. لا تُدرج أسعار أو كميات أو خصومات داخل اسم الصنف.\\n\"\n            \"5. الحروف باللغة العربية والإنجليزية السليمة فقط.\\n\"\n            f\"6. الرد يجب أن يكون كائن JSON صالح فقط: {{\\\"items\\\": [{{\\\"item_name_raw\\\": \\\"اسم الصنف بالضبط\\\", \\\"source_page\\\": {page_num}}}]}}\"\n        )\n\n        payload = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": prompt},\n                        {\n                            \"type\": \"image_url\",\n                            \"image_url\": {\n                                \"url\": f\"data:image/webp;base64,{img_b64}\"\n                            }\n                        }\n                    ]\n                }\n            ],\n            \"stream\": False\n        }\n\n        headers = {\n            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n        }\n\n        # 4. Send request with retry loop\n        success = False\n        for attempt in range(1, max_retries + 1):\n            t0 = time.time()\n            try:\n                print(f\"     [*] Sending Vision request to gateway (Attempt {attempt}/{max_retries})...\")\n                resp = requests.post(api_url, json=payload, headers=headers, timeout=240)\n                elapsed = time.time() - t0\n\n                if resp.status_code == 200:\n                    data = resp.json()\n                    raw_content = data.get(\"choices\", [{}])[0].get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\", \"\")\n                    parsed = _clean_json_response(raw_content)\n\n                    items = parsed.get(\"items\", [])\n                    # Verify page number\n                    for item in items:\n                        item[\"source_page\"] = page_num\n                        item[\"source_file\"] = filepath.name\n\n                    # Save to page result cache\n                    with open(page_res_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f_out:\n                        json.dump({\"page\": page_num, \"items\": items}, f_out, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n                    # Update manifest\n                    if page_num not in completed_set:\n                        completed_set.add(page_num)\n                    manifest[\"completed_pages\"] = sorted(list(completed_set))\n                    manifest[\"updated_at\"] = datetime.now().isoformat()\n                    with open(manifest_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f_m:\n                        json.dump(manifest, f_m, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n                    print(f\"     [+] [Page {page_num}] Succeeded in {elapsed:.1f}s -> {len(items)} items extracted.\")\n                    success = True\n                    break\n                else:\n                    print(f\"     [!] [Page {page_num}] HTTP Error {resp.status_code}: {resp.text[:200]}\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"     [!] [Page {page_num}] Exception on attempt {attempt}: {e}\")\n\n            time.sleep(2.0)\n\n        if not success:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to extract page {page_num} of {filepath.name} after {max_retries} attempts.\")\n\n    # All pages finished!\n    manifest[\"status\"] = \"completed\"\n    manifest[\"updated_at\"] = datetime.now().isoformat()\n    with open(manifest_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f_m:\n        json.dump(manifest, f_m, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n    # Collect and return all items\n    all_items = []\n    for p in range(1, total_pages + 1):\n        res_file = cache_dir / \"results\" / f\"page_{p}.json\"\n        if res_file.exists():\n            with open(res_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                p_data = json.load(f)\n                all_items.extend(p_data.get(\"items\", []))\n\n    print(f\"\\n[+] [VISION EXTRACTOR] Successfully completed all {total_pages} pages for {filepath.name}!\")\n    print(f\"[+] Total items extracted: {len(all_items)}\")\n    return all_items\n","Description":"Create gemini_vision_extractor.py for robust page-by-page vision extraction with resume and isolated cache","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy-vision\\src\\extract\\gemini_vision_extractor.py","toolAction":"Creating gemini_vision_extractor.py","toolSummary":"Write gemini_vision_extractor.py"}}]}
